From 2f6fa8fa11cd6465e54deb86eb0e6bbac4e47cfd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julian Cooper <115541810+Juliansgith@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:14:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 37/52] Path navigator: skip the step test for a candidate that
 cannot be occupied

TryAdvanceTargetPoint (0x005AF7E0) accepts a candidate path node only when
both CanOccupyTargetCell and the step test (CanReachCellFromCurrent or
CanPathCellTransition) hold. The binary evaluates the step test even when
the occupancy test already failed; its result is then never used, and both
step tests only read sim state (their grid gathers clear their marks
again), so it is skipped.

Verified with the same 30-minute all-AI checksum run as the previous change
(identical over all 18002 beats).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 3c1b95e9fdddcd25aa6c4c9332e3b25c53dec6a1)
(cherry picked from commit 931ee7563cac703a58f6d5e192e3bb8f1fab5424)
---
 src/sdk/moho/ai/CAiPathNavigator.cpp | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/sdk/moho/ai/CAiPathNavigator.cpp b/src/sdk/moho/ai/CAiPathNavigator.cpp
index a2c54101..0818cd61 100644
--- a/src/sdk/moho/ai/CAiPathNavigator.cpp
+++ b/src/sdk/moho/ai/CAiPathNavigator.cpp
@@ -1433,9 +1433,14 @@ bool CAiPathNavigator::TryAdvanceTargetPoint()
     // `COGrid::UnitIsBlocked`. The recovered form ran both unconditionally and
     // handed the short-step test `mCurrentPos` as its from-cell, which made it
     // a second swept mobile-unit test rather than the endpoint test it is.
-    const bool stepClear = (ManhattanDistance(mCurrentPos, candidate) > 1)
-      ? CanReachCellFromCurrent(*this, candidate)
-      : CanPathCellTransition(*this, candidate, candidate);
+    //
+    // The binary runs the step test even when `canOccupy` already failed; its
+    // result is then never used, and both step tests only read sim state (the
+    // grid gathers they make clear their marks again), so it is skipped here.
+    const bool stepClear = canOccupy &&
+      ((ManhattanDistance(mCurrentPos, candidate) > 1)
+         ? CanReachCellFromCurrent(*this, candidate)
+         : CanPathCellTransition(*this, candidate, candidate));
 
     if (canOccupy && stepClear) {
       mHasForwardProbe = 1;
